WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.132
Here’s how to track a drive and a walk with
Earth Odometer, even when your iPhone stays
home.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:09.346
On your iPhone, open Tracking and
permissions.

00:00:09.347 --> 00:00:14.140
Turn on automatic walking and Apple Health
distance, then allow access.

00:00:14.141 --> 00:00:17.599
For drives with your phone, enable automatic
drive tracking.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.462
In Journeys, choose an on-foot route and a
by-road route.

00:00:21.463 --> 00:00:23.622
Open each one and tap Start.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.399
You can have both going at once.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.965
Leaving your phone at home?

00:00:26.966 --> 00:00:31.921
Allow location on the Watch, then tap Start
outing before you leave.

00:00:31.922 --> 00:00:36.266
You can also start from your watch face, or
from a reminder you schedule.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:39.323
Drive to the trail, walk, and drive back.

00:00:39.324 --> 00:00:42.104
Leave the outing running through all three
legs.

00:00:42.105 --> 00:00:44.332
Tap End outing when you’re home.

00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:47.300
Reconnect your Watch and open Earth
Odometer.

00:00:47.301 --> 00:00:53.309
In this example, twenty road miles and three
walking miles add twenty-three to the
odometer.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.132
Each journey receives its matching miles.
